  "A1_results_paragraph": "At the patient level, the n=350 oncocytic-family cases differed substantially from the n=1192 conventional follicular family on demographics and management. Oncocytic patients were significantly older (mean 55.4 vs 51.0 years, Welch t-test p<0.001; Mann-Whitney U p<0.001), had larger dominant tumors among the 651 cases with size data (median 4.00 vs 3.10 cm, p<0.001), and underwent definitive total thyroidectomy at index at nearly twice the rate (38.3% vs 21.8%, p<0.001). Female predominance was similar in both families (71.7% vs 76.1%, p=0.111).",
